    "text": "A parallel plate capacitor is of area <math><mn>6</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and a separation <math><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The gap is filled with three dielectric materials of equal thickness (see figure) with dielectric constant <math><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The dielectric constant of a material which when fully inserted in above capacitor, gives same capacitance would be:<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/de098a67-37e3-4603-bbea-6d0aa08b56bf-image.png\" style=\"width: 325px; height: 136px;\" />",
